---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StatBar from '../components/StatBar.astro';
import GardenCTA from '../components/GardenCTA.astro';
import StackCards from '../components/StackCards.astro';
import Parallax from '../components/Parallax.astro';
import { SHOW_JOURNAL } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base hideGarden={true} title="About Eliana | The Soul Mami" description="Eliana, the Soul Mami, comes from a lineage of beekeepers, farmers, and storytellers. TEDx speaker, author of two books, facilitator of 200+ circles, and a life-liver, not a guru.">

  <!-- Beat: Positioning -->
  <section class="section hero">
    <div class="wrap grid-2" style="align-items:center;">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">The Human</span>
        <h1>Not a guru. A <em class="soul">life-liver.</em></h1>
        <p class="lead">
          I'm Eliana, aka the Soul Mami: mentor, facilitator, writer,
          TEDx speaker, music maker, and a highly curious student of
          this whole being-alive thing.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img class="photo photo--arch" src="/images/eliana-frame-1100.webp" srcset="/images/eliana-frame-600.webp 600w, /images/eliana-frame-1100.webp 1100w" sizes="(min-width: 861px) 504px, 100vw" width="1100" height="1467" alt="Eliana grinning through an empty vintage picture frame in a garden" style="max-height:480px;" fetchpriority="high" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beat: Proof -->
  <StatBar />

  <!-- From Lineage down, each section stacks over the last like a card. -->
  <div class="stack">

  <!-- Beat: Lineage -->
  <section class="section section--sand">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Lineage</span>
      <h2>My roots, and soil</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        I was born in the Dominican Republic, raised in New Jersey, and
        became fully alive as myself when I became a Global Citizen of
        the world. I've lived in 7 countries in the past decade and am
        constantly questioning what and where is home outside of myself.
      </p>
      <p>
        My roots are Afro, Taíno Indigenous and Caribbean. Ya tú sabe.
      </p>
      <p>
        I come from a lineage of storytellers, caretakers, farmers and
        nomads. The wisdom of cycles and beauty in simple living run
        through my veins. I come from honey, soil, prayer, cinnamon,
        tobacco, rivers and mountains, laughter, and documentarians of
        living life.
      </p>
      <p>
        Oh, and I wasn't supposed to be born. After 10 years of being told
        she would never be a mother, my mom prayed me into existence. I
        was her deepest desire and miracle child. She named me Eliana,
        meaning "My God has answered." Of course, she didn't know that
        then. Her intuition did.
      </p>
      <p>
        I grew up believing miracles are real and knowing an invisible
        force is alive, listening and always speaking. Childhood meant
        playing with cousins, gathering every weekend to commune, dance
        and hear stories from my tías and tíos. My roots are strong and
        well nourished.
      </p>
      <p>
        It's no wonder I believe we learn through story, movement,
        relationship, reflection and play. People aren't machines, and I
        refuse to treat you like one.
      </p>
      <p>
        What lights me up is seeing a seed in another human: curiosity
        wanting to live and grow. My life's work is creating spaces where
        that seed gets the sun, water and nourishment to evolve. Spaces
        where you feel more connected to yourself, each other and the
        work you're here to do.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beat: The Core -->
  <section class="section section--dark core">
    <picture class="core-bg" data-parallax>
      <source srcset="/images/circle-night.webp" type="image/webp" />
      <img src="/images/circle-night.jpg" alt="" width="1000" height="750" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </picture>
    <span class="core-shade" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="wrap prose center">
      <span class="eyebrow">The Core</span>
      <h2>Self-belonging is the whole thing.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Whatever The Soul Mami does, this is underneath it: do you know
        your soul? Do you know where you come from and why you are here?
        You are 1 of 1. There's stuff only you came here to express, and
        we need to see it, hear it and feel it.
      </p>
      <p>
        My dream is people living and enjoying life because they know
        who they are. Giving that self to themselves, and to the world.
        In a world that profits from your self-forgetting, remembering
        who you are is a radical act. I believe in magic, in the
        unknown, in miracles. And I believe in you being the one
        you've been waiting for.
      </p>
      <p class="lead"><em class="soul">How can we feel more alive?</em> That's the question I build everything around.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beat: Alchemy -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid-2" style="align-items:center;">
      <img class="photo" src="/images/eliana-dance.jpg" alt="Eliana dancing barefoot in a yellow dress, bathed in golden studio light" loading="lazy" />
      <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Alchemy</span>
      <h2>Bring me any emotion.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        I call myself an emotional alchemist because it's literal. Give
        me any emotion and I will feel it, transmute it and translate it.
        Emotions are visitors, each carrying a message.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before becoming this whole version of me, I was the teased girl,
        the fat girl, the nerd, the unchosen lover, the shy girl afraid to
        speak, the people pleaser, perfectionist, overachiever, the
        judgmental church girl, and the sensual woman afraid to be seen.
      </p>
      <p>
        Until I died to my artificial masks and was reborn as all of me.
        I'm comfortable with death and rebirth. When you're with me, you
        get to be too.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/work-with-me/">Work with me</a>
        {SHOW_JOURNAL && <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/journal/">Read my journal</a>}
      </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beat: My Dharma/Mission -->
  <section class="section section--dark core dharma">
    <picture class="core-bg" data-parallax>
      <source srcset="/images/eliana-sunflower.webp" type="image/webp" />
      <img src="/images/eliana-sunflower.jpg" alt="Eliana with her eyes closed, smelling a sunflower" width="1600" height="1202" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </picture>
    <span class="core-shade" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="wrap prose center">
      <span class="eyebrow">My Dharma/Mission</span>
      <figure class="dharma-quote">
        <blockquote>
          <p>“It is the pleasure of the bee to get the honey of the flower but it is also the pleasure of the flower to yield its honey to the bee. To the bee, the flower is a fountain of life, and to the flower, a bee is a messenger of love.”</p>
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption>: Kahlil Gibran</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beat: Fun facts -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid-2" style="align-items:start;">
      <div>
        <h2>Fun facts</h2>
        <ul class="facts-list">
        <li>I'm a cinnamon, rose and sandalwood type of girl</li>
        <li>The smell of burning wood reminds me of my childhood</li>
        <li>I like to walk barefoot when I'm home. No shoes in the house</li>
        <li>I started writing when I was 12. Had no idea I was an artist till adulthood</li>
        <li>I had sex for the first time at the age of 29. Yup, I know</li>
        <li>The sound of drums makes me wind my waist, always</li>
        <li>I don't want to have children in this lifetime and I'm at peace with it</li>
        <li>I'm a 2/4 Pure Sacral Generator (for my Human Design peeps)</li>
        <li>Virgo Sun, Taurus Moon, Sag Rising and Venus in Scorpio so I care DEEPLY</li>
        <li>I really love my solitude. Being alone, near a river and nature really feeds me</li>
        <li>The bee is my spirit animal. It's also the guide and soul of my business</li>
        <li>I received my calling when I was 18 and started my business at 24 after a series of dreams and messages from my inner voice</li>
        <li>I've been a licensed minister and preacher, a motivational speaker, author, dance facilitator, interpreter, news writer and producer, speech judge, kindness ambassador, mentor, and so much more</li>
        <li>I've built schools in Kenya and Haiti, ran medical clinics in slums, stayed in elephant sanctuaries in Thailand, met with underground groups in El Salvador and danced with little girls in Vietnam through the international trips I've hosted</li>
        <li>99% of the time, I have no idea what I'm doing, but intuitively I move in alignment</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <img class="photo photo--arch facts-photo" src="/images/eliana-colombia-1100.webp" srcset="/images/eliana-colombia-600.webp 600w, /images/eliana-colombia-1100.webp 1100w" sizes="(min-width: 861px) 504px, 100vw" width="1100" height="1361" alt="Eliana dancing barefoot in a yellow dress against a golden wall" loading="lazy" style="max-height:480px;" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <GardenCTA />

  </div>
  <StackCards />
  <Parallax />

</Base>

<style>
  .hero { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) var(--space-section); }
  .cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.9rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }

  /* The Core: full-screen night-circle photo, parallax, under a warm dark shade */
  .core {
    position: relative; /* becomes sticky inside the card stack */
    isolation: isolate;
    overflow: hidden;
    min-height: 100vh;
    min-height: 100svh;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    background: #140d08;
  }
  :global(.stack--on) > .core { position: sticky; }
  .core > .wrap { width: 100%; }
  .core-bg {
    position: absolute;
    /* Taller than the section: the extra is the parallax travel, hidden by overflow. */
    inset: 0 0 -18% 0;
    z-index: -2;
    will-change: transform;
  }
  .core-bg img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 30%;
  }
  /* Small caps over a photo: the lighter amber keeps the eyebrow readable past the string lights. */
  .core .eyebrow { color: var(--amber); }
  .core-shade {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: -1;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 75% 70% at 50% 45%, rgb(20 13 8 / 0.9), rgb(20 13 8 / 0.62));
  }

  /* My Dharma/Mission: The Core's pattern, with a lighter shade so her face and the
     sunflower stay recognizable; a soft shadow keeps the quote readable over them. */
  .dharma .core-bg img { object-position: 8% 40%; }
  /* Narrow screens crop to a tall slice: center on where her face meets the sunflower. */
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .dharma .core-bg img { object-position: 34% 40%; } }
  .dharma .core-shade {
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 70% 65% at 50% 50%, rgb(20 13 8 / 0.7), rgb(20 13 8 / 0.35));
  }
  .dharma-quote { margin: 0; }
  .dharma-quote blockquote { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; }
  .dharma-quote blockquote p {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-synthesis: none;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.6vw, 2rem);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--cream);
    text-wrap: balance;
    text-shadow: 0 1px 12px rgb(20 13 8 / 0.65), 0 1px 3px rgb(20 13 8 / 0.5);
  }
  .dharma-quote figcaption {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--cream);
    text-shadow: 0 1px 8px rgb(20 13 8 / 0.6);
  }

  /* Fun facts */
  .facts-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .facts-list li {
    padding: 0.85rem 0 0.85rem 1.9rem;
    position: relative;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sand-deep);
  }
  .facts-list li::before {
    content: "✦";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--honey);
  }
  .facts-photo { height: auto; object-position: 60% 12%; }
</style>
